-| Profile card | `.profile-card`, `.profile-card-band`, `.profile-card-head`, `.profile-card-body`, `.profile-identity`, `.profile-identity-name`, `.profile-identity-badges`, `.profile-identity-handle` | The avatar overlaps the color band. The display name sits to the right of the avatar, the role badges (the base role and a custom role if there is one) right next to the name, and the @username below the name (`13-profile.js buildProfileIdentity`). If the name is long the badges wrap to the next line, and if the card is narrower than 18rem the name, badges and @username move below the avatar. The two preview cards in Settings and the head of the avatar menu use the same layout. If the person has a cover photo it sits inside the band (`.profile-card-band.has-cover`, `.profile-card-cover`, `object-fit: cover`), and since the band is not positioned the avatar that overlaps it stays above the cover. In Turquoise the band and the cover keep the arch shape. |
+| Profile card | `.profile-card`, `.profile-card-band`, `.profile-card-head`, `.profile-card-body`, `.profile-identity`, `.profile-identity-name`, `.profile-identity-badges`, `.profile-identity-handle` | The avatar overlaps the color band. The display name sits to the right of the avatar, the role badges (the base role and a custom role if there is one) right next to the name, and the @username below the name (`13-profile.js buildProfileIdentity`). If the name is long the badges wrap to the next line, and if the card is narrower than 18rem the name, badges and @username move below the avatar. The two preview cards in Settings and the head of the avatar menu use the same layout. If the person has a cover photo it sits inside the band (`.profile-card-band.has-cover`, `.profile-card-cover`, `object-fit: cover`), and the avatar that overlaps it (`.avatar-wrap`, `position: relative`) comes after the band in the tree, so it is drawn above the cover. In Turquoise the band and the cover keep the arch shape. |
